    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0098" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg50"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1500.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 21, 1867.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In connection with your dispatch No. 2105,
                    of the 2d instant, I have the honor to report the receipt from Mr. West of an
                    official copy of the report of Colonel Warren’s trial, obtained by him, under my
                    directions, from the authorities in Ireland.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




